From 09ec7f26ab68fe137be5300119e0ffa68dd31867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 14:07:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08116/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-6071: the inert-probe
 lever cuts its target class 54% and does not move progress

The 2026-08-02 action census named the largest AVOIDABLE class: probes after which the
raw frame is byte-identical -- 19.1% of a 240-action budget, 18.4% at 2000. A node's
`untested` list is built once per node, so two nodes showing the same object each pay
separately for the same click; the most-repeated inert label was probed 356 times in one
run. An exact (action_id, x, y) already watched doing nothing, and never watched doing
anything, is inert again at 98.4% precision / 71.7% recall over 43,533 probe actions.

Built, DEFAULT OFF (`SUBMITTED_INERT_LABEL_DEFER_ENABLED = False`,
`CARNOT_ARC_INERT_LABEL_DEFER=1` to arm): an online per-run memory keyed on the LITERAL
action, learning from `_ingest`'s unconditionally-maintained unmasked frame hash. It
never drops a row -- it changes only which row a node pops next, and abstains entirely
once every remaining row is deferrable, so `_node_has_open_tier`, the frontier schedule
and the node's drain time are untouched. Three axes of difference from the RETIRED
`InertClickSigPruner` (key, consequence, learning channel) are in the module docstring.

Measured, 3 arms x 25 games x 3 seeds, budget 2000, offline arcade, LLM off, no GPU,
0 missing observations, adversarial-verify clean:

  A/A noise floor  75/75 identical traces -- the agent is DETERMINISTIC here, so every
                   treatment divergence is causal, not sampled
  target class     9,208 -> 4,239 actions (-54.0%), 13 games better / 1 worse, p=0.0018
  live 400-budget  games banking a level 3 -> 6 (ft09 x59.5, lp85 x9.0, su15 x2.5 on
                   the first level's score)
  levels @2000     14 -> 13.  NULL, and cd82 loses one at BOTH evidence floors
  hv progress      flat (1 better, 1 worse)
  states           p = 0.79.  NULL
  navigation       12,146 -> 13,903, 12 games worse, p = 0.013.  SIGNIFICANTLY WORSE

Every pre-registered progress axis is null. With only 1 discordant game the design could
not have reached p<0.05 on the primary axis -- stated up front, not discovered after. The
seed axis is decorative (0 of 25 games differ across seeds; the run seed does not reach
the explorer's frontier RNG). Recommendation: DO NOT flip the default. Next is a
live-budget (400-action) A/B where the primary axis is reachable, plus cd82.

Two process failures recorded rather than quietly fixed:
 * the FIRST A/B corpus was DISCARDED, not repaired. A ~20s source hot-swap during a
   background run contaminated 7 of 225 cells; those 7 are the ones that ANNOUNCED it,
   a flag-off cell in the same window would have been silent, so the set could not be
   bounded. Re-run with the source sha256 pinned before and after.
 * the level-up SACRED veto was DECORATIVE when written -- deleting it left the suite
   GREEN. Found by mutation, not by reading; now independently tested. 6/6 mutations
   killed, sources restored byte-identically.

Default-OFF inertness proven by differential: git HEAD's agent swapped into THIS checkout
and all 25 games re-run -- 25/25 byte-identical action traces. That backs the
`provenance.freshness_acknowledgements` added to the 12 artifacts the freshness lint
flagged (insertions only). A git-WORKTREE differential does NOT work for this agent: a
fresh worktree lacks untracked assets the live path reads and diverges on 19 of 25 games.

